{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["My face will go — I Myself will go, as you asked, as it is written: ופניך הולכים בקרב." "And I will give you rest — I will go with you to conquer the land, until I give you rest from all your enemies around, as it is written: עד אשר יניח ה׳ לאחיכם ככם; והיה בהניח ה׳ אלהיך לך מכל אויבך וגו׳. And the one who explains 'and I will give you rest' as 'I will give you peace of mind' — as though [saying] 'I will do as you asked' — that is folly! For then every matter about which the Holy One, blessed be He, would acquiesce to Moshe's request, He would say to him 'and I will give you rest' — but that would be a superfluous expression for no reason at all, and it is not the language of wisdom."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:50.828433085Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}